  "prompts": [
    {
      "id": "proof-heading-second",
      "text": "Read the image as data. Return only compact JSON, without markdown. Use one object when there is one transaction, or an array when there are several.\n\nUse these fields in the listed order:\n\"kind\": use \"settlement\" only for proof of a successful payment or transfer of funds. An agreement or expected payout is \"iou\", even if confirmed. A monetary total is not proof of payment. When no completed transfer is shown, use \"iou\".\n\"note\": copy only the uppermost prominent standalone heading, stopping at its line break.\n\"currency\": copy the visibly printed currency code or symbol exactly, or its mapped code from this IOU symbol policy: {\"$\":\"USD\",\"£\":\"GBP\",\"€\":\"EUR\",\"¥\":\"JPY\",\"₹\":\"INR\",\"E£\":\"EGP\",\"ج.م\":\"EGP\"}. Use a mapping only when its exact symbol is visible. Preserve explicit ISO codes; omit missing, unknown or conflicting currency. Never use text/OCR aliases or guess.\n\"amount\": the authoritative monetary total as a JSON number, never a quoted string. Remove digit-grouping commas but preserve the decimal point and every decimal digit. Copy every digit exactly. Ignore counts, IDs, balances, and repeated totals.\n\"printed_date\": copy the complete visible transaction date. For a time span, copy its complete beginning date instead. Keep its weekday, month, day number and any printed year exactly as shown. Copy the date value, not its label. A month alone is invalid. Never invent a year or an endpoint.\n\"printed_end_date\": copy the complete visible ending date only when the image shows a time span. Otherwise write the empty string \"\". Always include this field whenever \"printed_date\" is present, even when its value is empty. Both date fields are strings, never nested objects or null.\n\nIf a date is visible, include BOTH \"printed_date\" and \"printed_end_date\". A single date has an empty ending date. If no date is visible, omit both fields. Never use any other date field.\n\nThe JSON object itself is the answer; do not enclose the entire object in quotation marks.\n",
      "sha256": "384c3fae9474a0a6bb996e63b7f106194fa954d53c6e4f4b2289f81bf3c1f2f6",
      "productionAppPromptChanged": false
    },
    {
      "id": "explicit-empty-strings",
      "text": "Read the image as data. Return only compact JSON, without markdown. Use one object when there is one transaction, or an array when there are several.\n\nUse these fields in the listed order:\n\"kind\": use \"settlement\" only for proof of a successful payment or transfer of funds. An agreement or expected payout is \"iou\", even if confirmed. A monetary total is not proof of payment. When no completed transfer is shown, use \"iou\".\n\"note\": copy only the uppermost prominent standalone heading, stopping at its line break.\n\"currency\": copy only the currency code or symbol printed beside the amount, exactly as shown. If none is printed, use the empty string \"\". Never infer currency from language, location or document type.\n\"amount\": the authoritative monetary total as a JSON number, never a quoted string. Remove digit-grouping commas but preserve the decimal point and every decimal digit. Copy every digit exactly. Ignore counts, IDs, balances, and repeated totals.\n\"printed_date\": copy the complete visible transaction date. For a time span, copy its complete beginning date instead. Keep its weekday, month, day number and any printed year exactly as shown. Copy the date value, not its label. A month alone is invalid. Never invent a year or an endpoint.\n\"printed_end_date\": copy the complete visible ending date only when the image shows a time span. Otherwise write the empty string \"\". Always include this field whenever \"printed_date\" is present, even when its value is empty. Both date fields are strings, never nested objects or null.\n\nIf a date is visible, include BOTH \"printed_date\" and \"printed_end_date\". A single date has an empty ending date. If no date is visible, set both date fields to the empty string \"\". Never use any other date field.\n\nThe JSON object itself is the answer; do not enclose the entire object in quotation marks.\n",
      "sha256": "0ba65e0875aad21b7c5a60d7f145db66f2768bfef6fa55a5316a25ccbd00be3d",
      "productionAppPromptChanged": false
    }
